"Call for records pertaining to the Service Records of the Applicants, peruse the same and set-aside Notice Dated 18-01-2018 bearing No.Am/Aa/23/2017-18 issued by fourth respondent vide Annexure A-11. & Notice dated 07-12-2017 bearing No.SaAaSam/FSSA/C/85/2017-18 issued against the second Applicant issued by fifth respondent vide Annexure A-12 in the interest of justice and equity;
 ii. Issue a writ of certiorari quashing the order dated  30-06-2017 bearing  No.SaAasam/FSSA/C/08/2017-18 as the said Mr Somesh Olekar vs State Of Karnataka on 6 March, 2023 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/119949347/
7 order is basis for recovery proceedings passed by second respondent Vide Annexure A-15 only in so far as the applicants are concerned in the interest of justice and equity.

iii. Issue a writ of mandamus directing the Respondents to continue to pay the existing pay- scale i.e., Rs.21,600/- to Rs.40,050/- which is already fixed and received by the applicants;
iv. Direct the Respondents to extend the new pay scale as per C & R to the posts held by the applicants i.e., Rs.22,800/- to Rs.43,200/- and consequently release the arrears of salary from 01-06-2013, in the interest of justice and equity."
